## License boundaries

The MIT license applies to original integration code, installers, tests and
documentation in this repository. Original code generated with AI is also MIT
licensed when it is original work by this project.

It does not relicense upstream code. The following remain under their own
licenses, as marked by their source files:

* `driver/`: GPL-2.0 / GPL-2.0-or-later; see `driver/LICENSE`.
* `audio/`: GPL-2.0-only / GPL-2.0-or-later; see `audio/upstream/LICENSE` and
  the included kernel license texts.
* `wifi/dkms/`: ISC; see `wifi/dkms/LICENSE.ISC` and source SPDX headers.

Ubuntu's Broadcom firmware is downloaded from Ubuntu at installation time and
is not included or redistributed by this repository. Community board data is
also fetched separately; this repository does not grant additional rights to
that data.
